# Fingerprints of findings that are already on develop (or in the tree), have
# been rotated, and cannot be removed. Nothing else belongs here.
#
# - One entry per line, each with a comment linking its rotation issue.
# - Tree scan (gitleaks dir) fingerprints are file:rule:line. Commit scan
#   fingerprints are commit:file:rule:line, and only a commit on develop
#   qualifies: its squash SHA is stable.
# - Never ignore a finding on a pull request branch. Rotate the credential
#   first, then rebuild the branch. A pull request is scanned with the base
#   branch's copy of this file, so an entry added here takes effect only after
#   it merges. See docs/04-operations/github-security-runbook.md once it lands.
# - The reviewed fixtures that look like secrets are allowlisted in
#   .gitleaks.toml by file, rule and exact value, not here.
